WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.602 line:0%
-I am and have always been
a normal homosexual man

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:07.139 line:0%
who does all the normal things
normal homosexual men do.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:11.110 line:0%
-Like what?
-Well, I'll tell you.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.213 line:0%
♪ I wake up, drink my coffee ♪

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.748 line:0%
♪ Have brunch around 11 ♪

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:20.319 line:0%
♪ Walk my Bichon-Frisé,
then nap till half past seven ♪

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.488 line:0%
♪ A night out at the symphony ♪

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:24.858 line:0%
♪ Such elegance, what poise? ♪

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:28.928 line:0%
♪ Or maybe I'll just stay at
home with my two Sewer Boys ♪

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.096 line:0%
-What?

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:33.299 line:0%
-♪ The answer
is perfectly clear ♪

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:39.372
♪ It's a gay old life
being queer ♪

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.608
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.176
We're here with Nathan Lane.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:46.613
That was a clip
from "Dicks: The Musical."

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.914
-Yes.
-And this is a story

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:51.751
about separated twins.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:54.887
-Yes. It's a --
it is a deeply silly,

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:56.255
satirical, absurdist,

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:59.125
R-rated queer musical
based on "The Parent Trap."

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.794
-There we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.097
-And, you know,
it's not for everybody.

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:06.532
It's for -- It's for the gay
and the --

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.134
and the --
and the open minded.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.570
It's for the demented
and depraved.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.137
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.137 --> 00:01:14.574
It is the cinematic enema

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:18.911
America has been
so desperate for.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:23.916
So, you know, I would say have
an edible or two and run,

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:28.621
don't walk to catch
some "Dicks: The Musical."

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:32.692
-[ Laughs ] Now, in the clip,
you referenced the Sewer Boys,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:36.095
and I'm glad you brought them

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.163
because we don't see them
in the clip.

00:01:38.163 --> 00:01:40.366
-I know
-And I -- they really,

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.702
no offense,
they kind of steal the show.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:43.903
-Oh, totally.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.238
And it's all anyone's
talking about

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.839
aside from Taylor Swift,
the Sewer Boys.

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.708
-So, do you want to set up
the Sewer Boys?

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:53.480
-The Sewer Boys are -- are --
are these creatures

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.415
I captured, obviously
in the sewer,

00:01:56.415 --> 00:02:00.186
and I take them into my home
and they're like rescue dogs

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.521
and I keep them in a cage
in my living room.

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:06.459
[ Clears throat ] And I feed
them sort of like a mother bird.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:10.129
They like deli meat,
so I chew up ham

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:12.799
and I spit it into their mouths.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.267
You know, like their mother.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.268
-When doing that is
an award-winning actor...

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:17.403
-Yes.
-...what's going

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:18.737
through your head?

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:22.876
-Well, you know, when -- when we
talked about this,

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:25.411
at first when
they brought them out,

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.481
most of the budget went into
these puppets, by the way.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.217
And when they brought them out,
I said, this looks like someone

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.153
stole a Halloween display
from Walmart.

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:36.289
This can't possibly
be the real thing.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.924
And they said,
"Oh, no, don't worry,

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.258
we're just getting started."

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:40.760
And then they put
diapers on them.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.162
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:45.131
So these are my --
my Sewer Boys.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:48.200
-Alright.
There's...

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:54.307
-And -- and as you can see,
they -- they -- they --

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.374
they wear diapers.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:56.876
In the sewer,
they didn't have to.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:03:00.746
-I want to tell you,
it's a wonderful thing.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:02.414
First of all, there's so much
heavier than they look.

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:06.352
-Right? Me too.
-And...

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.854
-Oh, they -- they wear
ankle bracelets as well.

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:10.456
-And their -- their names.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.458
I think this is the litmus test.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.427
They're disgusting,
aren't they?

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.262
I think the litmus test
for this movie

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:19.565
are the names of the Sewer Boys
are Backpack and whisper.

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.970
-Now -- now, if you think
that's funny,

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.506
this is the movie for you.

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:29.942
And and if not, then you should
probably stay home

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.744
and watch that marathon
of "Blue Bloods."

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.179
-Yes.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.747
Now, I do want
to say one thing before.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.215
You were very nice and said

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:37.616
let's bring the Sewer Boys
on the show.

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:38.618
-Yeah.
-And we had to send --

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:39.652
because they're very heavy.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.953
We couldn't ask you
to bring them,

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:42.288
so we spent a production
assistant.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.656
-They don't really live with me.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.224
-Yeah, that's true.
-Yeah.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.059
They were --
they were at age A24.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.161
-Yeah. So we sent a production
assistant to get them.

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:50.763
-Yeah. And what happened?
-And she brought them

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.598
